Large positive responses mark list continuation and the '_replace' identifier
fragment. Smaller positives recognize retrieval, presence tests, filesystem
helpers, and size inspection. Setters, prototypes and stringification are
negative. A few enumeration-related words have weak positive responses. Unrecognized tokens get zero;
this is not a claim that one semantic category explains the entire component.
"""
READS = ()

DOM_LOOKUP = {
    '.getElementById', '.getElementsByClassName', '.getElementsByTagName',
    '.querySelector', '.querySelectorAll',
}
PRESENCE_TESTS = {
    '.exists', '.isPresent', '.isNotEmpty', '.IsNullOrEmpty',
